// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Numbers, text and bytes
// Demonstrates: radix and separated literals, the Int/Real
// libraries, scalar versus grapheme views of a Str, and ⌭ bytes.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

mask ≔ ⊓(0xFF)(0b1010_1010)
scaled ≔ ⋘(1)(10) ✚ ⋆(2)(8)
hypot ≔ √(⋇(3.0)(2.0) ✚ ⋇(4.0)(2.0))

// "e" + combining acute is two scalars but one grapheme.
word ≔ "e\u{301}👍"
scalars ≔ #(⇋(⍂(word)))
graphemes ≔ #(⇋(⌶(word)))

packed ≔ ⌭⍪(⌭⌘("obk"))(⌭⇋([0, 255]))
decoded ≔ ⌭⍕(⌭⌷(0)(3)(packed))

result ≔ mask ✚ scaled ✚ ↘(hypot) ✚ scalars ✚ graphemes ✚ ⌭#(packed)
❧
